Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: babysit
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, tar, gzip
Description: run a command detached, log it, and return early if it stalls
 babysit runs a command in the background under a babysitter process, echoes
 its output and writes it to a per-process log. It returns early when an
 expected line appears, when the command stops producing output, or after a
 timeout, and leaves the command running in every case.
 .
 babysitd is an optional systemd user service that archives the logs of
 past days, packs sooner when the disk fills up and expires old logs.
